WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:03.169
I'm just intensely

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.172
curious about people and social behavior.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.092
Everything that I'm doing
is just my way of satisfying

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:12.095
that curiosity.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:15.849
My work as a photographer

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.852
is deeply rooted in culture.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:22.981
I'm really excited to travel to Fort Worth

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.609
to explore all the old Western traditions
that make the city what it is.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:30.447
Okay, this is where the magic starts.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.407
Can I take some pictures
as you’re doing it? Sure.

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.117
Absolutely.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.037
When I start shooting a project,
I just like to arrive in a place

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.706
and really just follow my intuition.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.333
I don't really have a plan.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.336
That's very exciting, actually.

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:55.180
I'm most excited to photograph
the longhorn cattle drive,

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:58.767
which I've only heard about,
and it's one of the most unique traditions

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.228
in Fort Worth.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:05.440
Good morning.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.443
I'm Kristin. Welcome to Fort Worth.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:11.529
Have you been around Texas
longhorn cattle before?

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:12.781
Never.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:15.325
Everything that I've seen,
it's been almost a little surreal.

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:19.245
I've never seen this in real life.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.623
I’ve seen it only in Western movies.

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:25.126
But what's unique about their breed
is they're all different colors,

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:26.419
different sizes.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.921
He's a miniature steer.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.924
He's actually our 2022 world champion
miniature.

00:01:32.842 --> 00:01:34.344
It's very distinguished.

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:36.221
Some of their horns are going up.

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:39.224
Some are straight out. Some are twisting.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.684
And they grow
throughout their entire life.

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:44.979
So they're just
magnificent steers.

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:48.525
I didn't realize the horns
are going to be so huge and so beautiful.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:52.028
They're bigger than life huge.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:54.572
And we'll go out the gray gate.

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:57.909
The reason why we do this is we're
commemorating a time in history

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:01.329
when Longhorns were driven
through Fort Worth along what's called

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:04.332
the Chisholm Trail.

00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:12.006
So we're preserving Western heritage,
the American cowboy,

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:21.349
and, of course, the Texas Longhorn.

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:25.270
Joining the herd today is really just
an incredible experience to witness.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.399
Thank you.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:29.983
My pleasure.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.986
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:34.988
I mean, one of my favorite things
about travel

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.991
is that it opens my eyes
to new experiences and new cultures.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.829
That was amazing to watch.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.540
It was like a dance.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.960
I really can't wait to get back to Texas
and have more adventures here.

